 The primary application is very simple: 
  internal static class Program
{
    private static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Console.WriteLine(&quot;Hello, World!&quot;);
    }

    internal static int Add2(int a, int b) =&gt; a + b;
}

 The xUnit project is also simple: 
  using Xunit;
using LearnXUnit;

namespace LearnXUnit.Test
{
    public class UnitTest1
    {
        [Fact]
        public void Test2()
        {
            // Arrange
            int a = 2;
            int b = 3;

            // Act
            int bozo = LearnXUnit.Program.Add2(a, b);

            // Assert
            Assert.Equal(5, bozo);
        }
    }
}

 However, VS 2022 doesn't like  LearnXUnit.Program.Add2(a, b) . It complains that  Program  doesn't exist in  LearnXUnit . I've asked GitHub Copilot about this. But it insists of my putting this into  LearnXUnit 's project file: 
  &lt;ItemGroup&gt;
    &lt;InternalsVisibleTo Include=&quot;LearnXUnit.Test&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/ItemGroup&gt;

 However, whenever I put that XML into the project file, VS 2022 will always complain that I'm trying to introduce a circular reference between the two projects. However, GH Copilot always goes back to that solution, and I've asked it three times. 
 So, how to I make the xUnit test project reference the  Add2  method in the primary project?

